[
  {"comment": "Mortise and Tenon (mitcad#1012) with analytic volumes, on pairs of crossing boards: a rail 100 long to x = 0, 20 across and 60 high (120000), its end face side1 at x = 0, and a post 40 x 40 x 100 (160000) from x = 0 on, across the rail's end. The tenon's width runs along the end face's longest edge (the rail's height), centred. The mortise is the tenon grown by the clearance (0.1 mm) on every side and past its tip, so its volume is the tenon's plus the clearance's."},
  {"comment": "A blind tenon 40 x 8, 25 long (Box1 F1 Body1, Box2 F2 Body2, MortiseTenon1 F3): the rail gains 40 8 25 = 8000; the post loses 40.2 8.2 25.1 = 8273.964 = 8000 + 273.964 of clearance. Both bodies keep their names."},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
    "corner": [-100, 0], "length": 100, "width": 20, "height": 60, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
    "corner": [0, -10], "length": 40, "width": 40, "height": 100, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "mortise_tenon", "body": "F1.b0", "face": "F1:side1",
    "mortise_body": "F2.b0", "width": 40, "thickness": 8, "length": 25}},
  {"expect": {"feature": "MortiseTenon1", "status": "ok"}},
  {"expect": {"bodies": 2}},
  {"expect": {"body": "Body1", "volume": 128000, "tolerance": 1e-9, "has_face": "F3:side(c1[c4,c2])",
    "min": [-100, 0, 0], "max": [25, 20, 60]}},
  {"expect": {"body": "Body2", "volume": 151726.036, "tolerance": 1e-9, "has_face": "F3:side(c11[c14,c12])",
    "min": [0, -10, 0], "max": [40, 30, 100]}},

  {"comment": "Edited to 30 long: both bodies built again, the rail 120000 + 40 8 30, the post 160000 - 40.2 8.2 30.1."},
  {"cmd": "edit_feature", "uid": "F3", "def": {"type": "mortise_tenon", "body": "F1.b0", "face": "F1:side1",
    "mortise_body": "F2.b0", "width": 40, "thickness": 8, "length": 30}},
  {"expect": {"feature": "MortiseTenon1", "status": "ok"}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F1.b0", "volume": 129600, "tolerance": 1e-9, "max": [30, 20, 60]}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F2.b0", "volume": 150077.836, "tolerance": 1e-9}},

  {"comment": "A through tenon (Box3 F4, Box4 F5, MortiseTenon2 F6): flush with the post's far face, 40 long: the rail gains 40 8 40 = 12800, the post loses 40.2 8.2 40 = 13185.6 = 12800 + 385.6 of clearance (the mortise runs on past the post)."},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
    "corner": [-100, 200], "length": 100, "width": 20, "height": 60, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
    "corner": [0, 190], "length": 40, "width": 40, "height": 100, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "mortise_tenon", "body": "F4.b0", "face": "F4:side1",
    "mortise_body": "F5.b0", "width": 40, "thickness": 8, "through": true}},
  {"expect": {"feature": "MortiseTenon2", "status": "ok"}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F4.b0", "volume": 132800, "tolerance": 1e-9}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F4.b0", "max": [40, 220, 60], "tolerance": 1e-6}},
  {"expect": {"body": "F5.b0", "volume": 146814.4, "tolerance": 1e-9, "max": [40, 230, 100]}},

  {"comment": "Rounded corners by a 6 mm tool (Box5 F7, Box6 F8, MortiseTenon3 F9): the mortise's corners round by 3, the tenon's edges by 3 - 0.1 = 2.9. The tenon (40 8 - (4 - pi) 2.9^2) 25 = 7819.519855; the mortise (40.2 8.2 - (4 - pi) 3^2) 25.1 = 8080.049780 = the tenon's plus 260.529925 of clearance."},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
    "corner": [-100, 400], "length": 100, "width": 20, "height": 60, "operation": "new_body"}},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "box", "plane": {"type": "origin", "plane": "xy"},
